      "id": "claim_1f0be67373a6407ba28a83ae52222018",
      "statement": "The baseline projection rolls CET1 forward as beginning CET1 plus net income (6,600 growing 0.8% per quarter) minus preferred dividends, common dividends (prior-quarter shares x $1.15) and buybacks (3,000 per quarter), plus other movements (-150); buybacks retire shares at a flat $262 price and RWA grows 1% per quarter, raising the CET1 ratio from 15.14% to 16.15% by Q3 2028.",
