    {
      "id": "claim_6688d80d546d46b790dbc4b68365573f",
      "statement": "The stress projection builds pre-tax income as PPNR minus provisions minus trading and counterparty losses (SUM(C7:C9)), taxes it at the 22% effective rate with a tax benefit recognised on losses, suspends buybacks (hard-coded 0, CCAR convention), holds common dividends flat at 1,588.15 per quarter because the share count does not shrink, and applies scenario RWA growth; the stress CET1 ratio bottoms at 12.90% in Q3 2027 and recovers to 13.63% by Q3 2028.",
